1
00:00:00,450 --> 00:00:01,891
Same laddoos inside.

2
00:00:01,891 --> 00:00:02,791
Two packs.

3
00:00:02,767 --> 00:00:05,619
One plain, one with the Laddoo Lab name.

4
00:00:05,919 --> 00:00:08,577
Parents still pick Laddoo
Lab, again and again.

5
00:00:09,127 --> 00:00:11,327
Why does a name change the choice?

6
00:00:11,327 --> 00:00:12,757
That is brand equity.

7
00:00:13,407 --> 00:00:17,109
Laddoo Lab now has a name, a
logo, and a pack people know.

8
00:00:17,459 --> 00:00:18,656
For months, Mrs.

9
00:00:18,656 --> 00:00:21,661
Rao has packed its laddoos
in her daughter's tiffin.

10
00:00:22,011 --> 00:00:23,586
She tells other parents.

11
00:00:23,586 --> 00:00:25,114
They tell more parents.

12
00:00:25,464 --> 00:00:28,502
Slowly, the name itself has
started to mean something.

13
00:00:29,152 --> 00:00:30,835
So what is brand equity?

14
00:00:31,135 --> 00:00:36,645
Kevin Lane Keller explained it in
the Journal of Marketing, in 1993.

15
00:00:36,995 --> 00:00:41,333
Brand equity is the differential
effect of brand knowledge on consumer

16
00:00:41,333 --> 00:00:44,032
response to the marketing of the brand.

17
00:00:44,382 --> 00:00:48,085
Differential effect simply means
the difference the brand makes.

18
00:00:48,435 --> 00:00:52,759
In simple words: same product, plus
a known name, gives an extra pull.

19
00:00:53,409 --> 00:00:55,499
Zoya runs a test at the school gate.

20
00:00:55,849 --> 00:00:57,411
First, a blind test.

21
00:00:57,411 --> 00:01:01,202
Two plain packs, A and B,
with the same laddoos inside.

22
00:01:01,552 --> 00:01:03,544
Twenty parents taste and choose.

23
00:01:03,894 --> 00:01:05,794
Ten pick A, and ten pick B.

24
00:01:05,794 --> 00:01:08,654
A dead heat, because the
laddoos are the same.

25
00:01:09,304 --> 00:01:10,686
Now the named test.

26
00:01:10,686 --> 00:01:13,893
Same laddoos again, but
one pack says Laddoo Lab.

27
00:01:14,243 --> 00:01:15,903
Twenty new parents choose.

28
00:01:16,253 --> 00:01:17,935
Sixteen pick Laddoo Lab.

29
00:01:17,935 --> 00:01:20,035
Only four pick the plain pack.

30
00:01:20,385 --> 00:01:22,734
Same taste, six extra choices.

31
00:01:22,734 --> 00:01:25,270
That gap is brand equity at work.

32
00:01:25,920 --> 00:01:27,476
Nani makes the laddoos.

33
00:01:27,476 --> 00:01:29,128
Customers make the brand.

34
00:01:29,828 --> 00:01:33,838
Keller showed that brand equity is
built like a pyramid, one step at a

35
00:01:33,838 --> 00:01:34,738
time.

36
00:01:34,688 --> 00:01:35,588
One.

37
00:01:35,210 --> 00:01:36,110
Identity.

38
00:01:35,987 --> 00:01:37,990
Do people know who you are?

39
00:01:37,990 --> 00:01:39,983
Parents can name Laddoo Lab.

40
00:01:40,283 --> 00:01:41,183
Two.

41
00:01:40,748 --> 00:01:41,648
Meaning.

42
00:01:41,395 --> 00:01:42,898
What do you stand for?

43
00:01:42,898 --> 00:01:45,376
A healthy sweet, with no refined sugar.

44
00:01:45,676 --> 00:01:46,576
Three.

45
00:01:46,275 --> 00:01:47,175
Response.

46
00:01:47,022 --> 00:01:49,095
What do people think and feel?

47
00:01:49,095 --> 00:01:51,826
They trust it, and feel good giving it.

48
00:01:52,126 --> 00:01:53,026
Four.

49
00:01:52,664 --> 00:01:54,431
Relationship, at the top.

50
00:01:54,431 --> 00:01:57,830
Loyal parents buy every
week, and tell their friends.

51
00:01:58,480 --> 00:02:02,027
David Aaker named five assets
that make up brand equity.

52
00:02:02,027 --> 00:02:04,437
Where do we see them at work today?

53
00:02:04,787 --> 00:02:05,687
Awareness.

54
00:02:05,601 --> 00:02:07,199
People know your name.

55
00:02:07,199 --> 00:02:10,195
Travellers spot an
airline's logo at a glance.

56
00:02:10,545 --> 00:02:11,769
Perceived quality.

57
00:02:11,769 --> 00:02:13,705
People expect it to be good.

58
00:02:13,705 --> 00:02:16,076
Patients trust a well known hospital.

59
00:02:16,426 --> 00:02:17,448
Associations.

60
00:02:17,448 --> 00:02:19,643
What the name brings to mind.

61
00:02:19,643 --> 00:02:22,433
A phone maker's name means smart design.

62
00:02:22,783 --> 00:02:23,683
Loyalty.

63
00:02:23,493 --> 00:02:25,182
People keep coming back.

64
00:02:25,182 --> 00:02:28,010
A bank keeps the same customers for years.

65
00:02:28,360 --> 00:02:29,477
Other assets.

66
00:02:29,477 --> 00:02:31,439
Things rivals cannot copy.

67
00:02:31,439 --> 00:02:34,299
A snack company registers its trademark.

68
00:02:34,949 --> 00:02:37,513
But is brand equity always good news?

69
00:02:37,513 --> 00:02:38,927
It cuts both ways.

70
00:02:39,277 --> 00:02:40,357
The good side.

71
00:02:40,357 --> 00:02:44,140
Trust makes buying easy, and
shops want to stock the brand.

72
00:02:44,490 --> 00:02:45,544
The hard side.

73
00:02:45,544 --> 00:02:49,155
It takes years to build, and
one bad batch can break it.

74
00:02:49,505 --> 00:02:53,061
Arjun wants to switch to a
cheaper ghee, to save money.

75
00:02:53,061 --> 00:02:54,082
Nani says no.

76
00:02:54,432 --> 00:02:56,636
Parents pay for the promise, she says.

77
00:02:56,636 --> 00:02:59,476
Break it once, and the name
stops meaning anything.

78
00:02:59,826 --> 00:03:04,618
And under the accounting rule I A S
38, a brand you build yourself is not

79
00:03:04,618 --> 00:03:07,629
even shown as an asset
on the balance sheet.

80
00:03:07,979 --> 00:03:08,929
The lesson?

81
00:03:08,929 --> 00:03:10,581
A brand is a promise.

82
00:03:10,581 --> 00:03:12,439
Keep it every single day.

83
00:03:13,089 --> 00:03:14,016
Quick check.

84
00:03:14,016 --> 00:03:18,738
Parents pick the named pack over a
plain one, with the same laddoos inside.

85
00:03:18,738 --> 00:03:19,770
What is this?

86
00:03:21,670 --> 00:03:22,710
Brand equity!

87
00:03:22,710 --> 00:03:25,952
The name adds value,
beyond the product itself.

88
00:03:26,552 --> 00:03:27,561
So, remember.

89
00:03:27,861 --> 00:03:32,215
Brand equity is the extra value
a known name adds to a product.

90
00:03:32,565 --> 00:03:37,041
It lives in people's minds: awareness,
quality, meaning and loyalty.

91
00:03:37,391 --> 00:03:41,429
It takes years to build and moments
to lose, so keep the promise.

92
00:03:42,029 --> 00:03:45,831
Next time, we'll explore pricing
objectives and strategies.
